  "tallyName": "Tally",
  "tallyTagline": "Cross out numbers until every line adds up",
  "tallyRules": "• Every cell holds a number. Cross some of them out.\n• The numbers left in each row and column must add up to the number outside the grid.\n\nTap a cell to cycle: crossed out → circled (your \"this one stays\" note) → empty. Long-press / right-click cycles back. Circles are optional: the puzzle is done once the right numbers are crossed out.",
  "tutTally1": "Cross out numbers so that the ones left in each row and column add up to the number outside. Tap a number once to cross it out. A 7 can't stay in a row that adds up to 2.",
  "tutTally2": "A number bigger than its row's or column's sum always goes. The highlighted 8 sits in a row that adds up to 6: cross it out, then finish the board.",
  "tutTally3": "The top row's numbers make 15, but it needs 12, so only the 3 can go: the 8 and the 4 must stay. Tap twice to circle a number that stays, then finish the board.",
  "tutTally4": "Now a real board. Start with lines whose sum is small, or close to the total of all their numbers.",
  "tutTallyS1": "Try every way to make a line's sum. A number used in every way stays, one used in none goes: 7 from 5, 4 and 3 can only be 4 + 3, so the 5 goes.",
  "tutTallyS2": "A hard board. When stuck, cross a number out and follow the sums: if some row or column can no longer add up, that number stays.",
