  "tagWater": "water, fill, liquid, pour, level, tank, pool, flood",
  "basinsName": "Basins",
  "basinsTagline": "Fill the basins with level water to match the counts",
  "basinsRules": "• The grid is cut into basins. Fill some cells with water.\n• Water settles: in every basin it fills from the bottom up to one level, the same across the whole basin. Every cell of the basin at that height or lower holds water, every cell above it stays dry. A basin may also stay empty or fill to the top.\n• The numbers outside the grid tell how many water cells each row and column holds.\n\nTap a cell to cycle: water → dry (your note) → empty. Right-click cycles back. Slide across cells to fill them all in one go. A long press lets the water settle: it fills every cell of a basin below your water, and marks dry the cells above your dry marks and in rows and columns that have all their water. Dry marks are optional: the puzzle is done once all the water is in place.",
  "tutBasins1": "The grid is cut into basins, and water settles in each one from the bottom up. The numbers outside tell how many water cells each row and column holds. Column A holds 2, so its basin fills its two lowest cells. Tap a cell to fill it with water, tap again to mark it dry.",
  "tutBasins2": "Water lies level across the whole basin: when one cell of a basin holds water, so does every cell of that basin as low or lower. Row 2 needs just one water cell, so the wide basin can't reach that high. Finish the board.",
  "tutBasins3": "Think ahead: water in a cell fills everything below it in its basin. Once the bottom row is full, column A needs just one more water cell, but water in its top cell would fill two. So the top cell stays dry. Finish the board.",
  "tutBasins4": "Now a real board. Start with rows and columns that are empty or full, let the water settle, and before you fill a cell, count how much water it brings along.",
  "tutBasinsS1": "Water in a row comes in pieces: the cells of one basin in that row fill together. When only some sets of pieces add up to the row's count, a piece that is in all of them holds water, and a piece in none of them stays dry.",
  "tutBasinsS2": "Try every water level of a basin, from empty to full, against the counts of the rows and columns it touches. Cells that come out the same in every level that fits are settled.",
  "tutBasinsS3": "A hard board: some counts are hidden. When stuck, suppose a cell holds water and let it settle: if a row or column overflows or can't reach its count, that cell stays dry.",
  "exBasinsSupposeWater": "Suppose {cell} held water.",
  "@exBasinsSupposeWater": {"placeholders": {"cell": {}}},
  "exBasinsSupposeDry": "Suppose {cell} stayed dry.",
  "@exBasinsSupposeDry": {"placeholders": {"cell": {}}},
