  "tagMemory": "memory, remember, recall, brain training, concentration, attention",
  "glimpseName": "Glimpse",
  "glimpseTagline": "Cells light up for a moment: tap them all from memory",
  "glimpseRules": "• Some cells light up for a moment, then go dark. Tap every cell that lit up, in any order.\n• Tap Ready to hide them sooner.\n• A tap on a cell that didn't light up ends the round.\n• A round you get right scores a point per cell, and the next one lights one more cell. After a miss, it lights one fewer.\n\nGoals\n• Rounds: play 10 rounds for a best score.\n• Lives: play on until your third miss.\n\nThe difficulty sets how many cells the first round lights and how long they stay lit.",
  "glimpsePrompt": "Tap every cell that lit up",
  "tutGlimpse1": "Tap the board to start. Three cells light up for a moment: remember them, and once they go dark, tap all three.",
  "tutGlimpse2": "Tap Ready as soon as you have the cells, to hide them sooner. A tap on a cell that didn't light up ends the round; here the round then plays again. Get both rounds right.",
  "tutGlimpse3": "A real board: each round you get right lights one more cell next time, and a miss lights one fewer. Get 3 rounds right.",
  "famMemory": "Memory",
  "famMemoryAbout": "Look closely, then answer from memory. Every round you get right makes the next one harder",
  "vanishName": "Vanish",
  "vanishTagline": "Tap 1 and the numbers hide: tap the rest in order from memory",
  "vanishRules": "• Numbers from 1 up appear on the grid. Take your time: they stay until you tap 1.\n• As soon as you tap 1, the other numbers hide. Tap their cells in order: 2, 3, 4…\n• A tap on the wrong cell ends the round.\n• A round you get right scores a point per number, and the next one shows one number more. After a miss, it shows one fewer.\n\nGoals\n• Rounds: play 10 rounds for a best score.\n• Lives: play on until your third miss.\n\nThe difficulty sets how many numbers the first round shows.",
  "vanishWatch": "Tap 1 when you're ready",
  "vanishPrompt": "Tap the numbers in order",
  "tutVanish1": "Tap the board to start. Numbers appear: tap 1, and the others hide. Then tap where 2 and 3 were.",
  "tutVanish2": "Look as long as you like: the numbers stay until you tap 1. A tap on the wrong cell ends the round; here the round then plays again. Get both rounds right.",
  "tutVanish3": "A real board: each round you get right shows one number more next time, and a miss one fewer. Get 3 rounds right.",
  "hopperName": "Hopper",
  "hopperTagline": "Watch the frog hop from pad to pad, then retrace its jumps",
  "hopperRules": "• A frog hops from pad to pad, one jump at a time. When it stops, tap the pads it landed on, in the same order.\n• A pad can come up more than once: tap it again each time.\n• A wrong tap ends the round.\n• A round you get right scores a point per jump, and the next one has one jump more. After a miss, it has one fewer.\n\nOrder\n• Same order: from the first jump to the last.\n• Backwards: from the last jump back to the first.\n\nGoals\n• Rounds: play 10 rounds for a best score.\n• Lives: play on until your third miss.\n\nThe difficulty sets how many jumps the first round has and how fast the frog hops.",
  "hopperOrder": "Order",
  "hopperForward": "Same order",
  "hopperForwardHint": "Tap the pads in the order the frog jumped.",
  "hopperReverse": "Backwards",
  "hopperReverseHint": "Tap the pads from the frog's last jump back to its first.",
  "hopperWatch": "Watch the frog…",
  "hopperPrompt": "Tap the pads in order",
  "hopperPromptReverse": "Tap the pads backwards, last jump first",
  "tutHopper1": "Tap the board to start. The frog hops from pad to pad. When it stops, tap the pads it landed on, in the same order.",
  "tutHopper2": "A pad can come up more than once: tap it again each time. A wrong tap ends the round; here the round then plays again. Get both rounds right.",
  "tutHopper3": "With the Backwards option, tap the same pads from the last jump back to the first. Try it once.",
  "tutHopper4": "A real board: each round you get right adds a jump next time, and a miss takes one away. Get 3 rounds right.",
  "reboundName": "Rebound",
  "reboundTagline": "Remember the bumpers, then tell where the ball comes out",
  "reboundRules": "• Bumpers sit on the grid, and a ball waits at an arrow on the edge. Remember the bumpers: after a moment (or when you tap Ready) they hide.\n• The ball rolls in at the arrow, and every bumper it meets turns it a quarter turn, the way the bumper slants. Tap the edge where it will leave the board.\n• A round you get right scores a point per bumper, and the next one has one bumper more. After a miss, it has one fewer.\n\nGoals\n• Rounds: play 10 rounds for a best score.\n• Lives: play on until your third miss.\n\nThe difficulty sets how many bumpers the first round has and how long they stay.",
  "reboundPrompt": "Tap where the ball leaves the board",
  "tutRebound1": "Tap the board to start. The ball rolls in at the arrow and bounces off the bumper, the way it slants. Remember it; when it hides, tap the edge where the ball comes out.",
  "tutRebound2": "The ball may meet several bumpers and miss others. Tap Ready as soon as you have them. A wrong edge ends the round; here the round then plays again.",
  "tutRebound3": "A real board: each round you get right adds a bumper next time, and a miss takes one away. Get 3 rounds right.",
  "pebblesName": "Pebbles",
  "pebblesTagline": "Two kinds of stones, each kind all in one piece",
  "pebblesRules": "• Put a stone in every cell: filled or hollow.\n• All filled stones form one group, joined side by side, and so do all hollow stones.\n• No 2×2 block holds four stones of one kind.\n• Some stones are shown from the start.\n\nTap a cell to cycle: filled → hollow → empty. Long-press / right-click cycles back. Slide across cells to put the same stone in all of them. Stones of one kind side by side are drawn joined, so you can see the groups.",
  "tutPebbles1": "Put a stone in every cell. All filled stones must form one group, joined side by side, and so must all hollow stones. Tap an empty cell once for a filled stone, twice for a hollow one. Fill in this board.",
  "tutPebbles2": "No 2×2 block may hold four stones of one kind. The highlighted block already has three hollow stones, so its last cell gets a filled one. Finish the board the same way.",
  "tutPebbles3": "Every group must reach the rest of its kind. The hollow stone in the corner is walled in but for one cell, so that cell gets a hollow stone too. Follow the hollow stones until they meet the others.",
  "tutPebbles4": "A cell surrounded by filled stones can't hold a hollow one: it would be cut off from the other hollow stones. The same goes the other way round. Fill the highlighted cell, then finish the board.",
  "tutPebbles5": "Now a real board. Look for blocks with three stones alike, and for groups with only one way out.",
  "tutPebblesS1": "Going round the edge of the board, the filled stones form one unbroken run and the hollow stones another: if the edge switched kinds four times, the two groups would have to cross. A1 and D4 hold filled stones and C4 a hollow one, so the edge from A1 along the top and down to D4 is all filled.",
  "tutPebblesS2": "A 2×2 block never alternates, with filled stones on one diagonal and hollow ones on the other: the filled pair could only meet by going round one of the hollow stones and cutting it off. So when one diagonal holds two stones alike and the other one stone of the other kind, the last cell matches the diagonal.",
  "tutPebblesS3": "Some cells hold a kind together: if the other kind took such a cell, the stones on either side of it could no longer meet. Such a cell gets the kind it holds together. Look for narrow passages between the groups.",
  "exPebblesBlock": "{cell} holds {stone}: the rest of its 2×2 block holds {other}, and a block never holds four alike.",
  "@exPebblesBlock": {"placeholders": {"cell": {}, "stone": {}, "other": {}}},
