  "totalsName": "Totals",
  "totalsTagline": "A crossword of digits that add up across and down",
  "totalsRules": "• Fill every empty cell with a digit from 1 to 9.\n• The clue cells give sums: the number above the diagonal is the sum of the run of cells to its right, the number below the diagonal the sum of the run below it. A run ends at the next clue cell or the edge.\n• A run never holds a digit twice.\n\nPick a digit in the palette and tap cells to place it, or tap a cell first and then a digit. The pencil button toggles small notes. Long-press / right-click clears a cell. A sum fades once its run is full and adds up.",
  "tutTotals1": "Fill the empty cells with digits 1 to 9. In a clue cell, the number above the diagonal is the sum of the run to its right, the number below it the sum of the run below. 3 in two cells can only be 1 + 2, and 4 only 1 + 3: the corner cell is in both runs, so it takes the 1.",
  "tutTotals2": "A run never holds a digit twice: 4 in two cells is 1 + 3, never 2 + 2. Fill in this board.",
  "tutTotals3": "Some sums can be made only one way: 24 in three cells needs 7, 8 and 9, and 7 in three cells needs 1, 2 and 4. Each cell takes a digit that both its runs allow.",
  "tutTotals4": "Now a real board. Start with the runs whose sum can be made only one way, then look where runs cross.",
  "tutTotalsS1": "List the sets of different digits that make a run's sum. A digit that is in every set has to go somewhere in the run: if only one cell of the run can take it, it goes there.",
  "tutTotalsS2": "Sometimes every digit fits a cell on its own, but not together with the others: if two cells of a run can only hold 1 or 3, they take both, and no other cell of the run can. Try every way to fill a short run with different digits.",
  "tutTotalsS3": "The hardest boards need a guess you can disprove. Suppose a cell holds one of its last two or three digits and follow on; if a run can no longer make its sum, cross the digit off.",
  "exTotalsCombo": "To make {sum} in {run}, the open cells can only hold {digits}, so {cell} can't be {gone}.",
  "@exTotalsCombo": {"placeholders": {"sum": {}, "run": {}, "digits": {}, "cell": {}, "gone": {}}},
  "exTotalsMust": "{cell} must be {value}: every way to make {sum} in {run} uses {value}, and no other cell there can take it.",
  "@exTotalsMust": {"placeholders": {"sum": {}, "run": {}, "value": {}, "cell": {}}},
  "exTotalsFill": "No way to fill {run} with different digits that make {sum} puts {gone} into {cell}.",
  "@exTotalsFill": {"placeholders": {"sum": {}, "run": {}, "gone": {}, "cell": {}}},
  "exTotalsNaked": "{cell} must be {value}: every other digit is ruled out there.",
  "@exTotalsNaked": {"placeholders": {"cell": {}, "value": {}}},
  "exTotalsFailEmpty": "But then no digit is left for {cell}.",
  "@exTotalsFailEmpty": {"placeholders": {"cell": {}}},
  "exTotalsFailRun": "But then {run} can no longer make {sum}.",
  "@exTotalsFailRun": {"placeholders": {"sum": {}, "run": {}}},
  "famSudoku": "Sudoku",
  "famSudokuAbout": "Every digit once per row, column and box, with more clues on top",
  "pocketsName": "Pockets",
  "pocketsTagline": "Sudoku whose dashed pockets add up to their sums",
  "pocketsRules": "• Fill every cell with a digit from 1 to N (N = grid size): each digit once in every row, every column and every box, as in Sudoku.\n• The grid is also cut into pockets with dashed outlines. The digits of a pocket add up to the number in its corner, and a pocket never holds a digit twice.\n• There are no given digits: the sums tell you everything.\n\nPick a digit in the palette and tap cells to place it, or tap a cell first and then a digit. The pencil button toggles small notes. Long-press / right-click clears a cell. A sum fades once its pocket is full and adds up.",
  "tutPockets1": "As in Sudoku, every row, column and box (the thick outlines) holds each digit from 1 to 4 once. The dashed pockets add more: their digits add up to the number in the corner. 3 in two cells can only be 1 + 2, and 7 only 3 + 4; the columns tell you which goes where.",
  "tutPockets2": "A pocket never holds a digit twice, even where its cells sit in different rows and columns. So three cells of a 4 × 4 leave out just one digit: 6 is 1 + 2 + 3, and 8 is 1 + 3 + 4.",
  "tutPockets3": "This board has no digits at all. Start with the pockets whose sum can be made only one way, then go on as in Sudoku.",
  "tutPockets4": "Now a real board. Note the digits a pocket can hold, and remember: a whole row, column or box adds up to 1 + 2 + … + 6 = 21.",
  "tutPocketsS1": "A whole row, column or box always adds up to the same total: 21 on a 6 × 6, 45 on a 9 × 9. Take away the sums of the pockets lying wholly inside it, and what is left is the sum of its other cells. When one or two cells are left over, that often settles them.",
  "tutPocketsS2": "It works the other way round too. Add up the pockets that reach into a row, column or box, take away its total, and you have the sum of their cells sticking out of it. Bands of whole boxes work just the same.",
  "tutPocketsS3": "The hardest boards need a guess you can disprove. Suppose a cell holds one of its last two or three digits and follow on; if a pocket can no longer make its sum, or a digit has no place left, cross the digit off.",
  "exPocketsCombo": "To make {sum} in the pocket at {pocket}, its open cells can only hold {digits}, so {cell} can't be {gone}.",
  "@exPocketsCombo": {"placeholders": {"sum": {}, "pocket": {}, "digits": {}, "cell": {}, "gone": {}}},
  "exPocketsMust": "{cell} must be {value}: every way to make {sum} in the pocket at {pocket} uses {value}, and no other cell there can take it.",
  "@exPocketsMust": {"placeholders": {"sum": {}, "pocket": {}, "value": {}, "cell": {}}},
  "exPocketsFill": "No way to fill the pocket at {pocket} with different digits that make {sum} puts {gone} into {cell}.",
  "@exPocketsFill": {"placeholders": {"sum": {}, "pocket": {}, "gone": {}, "cell": {}}},
  "exPocketsLineRow": "Every way to make {sum} in the pocket at {pocket} uses {value}, and there it can only go in row {row}, so {value} is ruled out in the rest of row {row}.",
  "@exPocketsLineRow": {"placeholders": {"sum": {}, "pocket": {}, "value": {}, "row": {}}},
  "exPocketsLineCol": "Every way to make {sum} in the pocket at {pocket} uses {value}, and there it can only go in column {col}, so {value} is ruled out in the rest of column {col}.",
  "@exPocketsLineCol": {"placeholders": {"sum": {}, "pocket": {}, "value": {}, "col": {}}},
