  "chambersName": "Chambers",
  "chambersTagline": "Shade each room's count, and keep the lines between rooms short",
  "chambersRules": "• The grid is cut into rooms. A number in a room tells how many of its cells are shaded; a room without a number may hold any count.\n• Shaded cells never touch side by side.\n• The unshaded cells form one connected area.\n• A straight line of unshaded cells, across or down, never crosses two room borders: it reaches into two rooms at most.\n\nTap a cell to cycle: shaded → dot (your \"this one stays\" note) → empty. Right-click cycles back. A long press dots the cells next to shaded ones and the rest of every room that has all its shaded cells. Dots are optional: the puzzle is done once the right cells are shaded.",
  "tutChambers1": "The grid is cut into rooms, and a number tells how many cells of its room are shaded. Shaded cells never touch side by side. A room with 0 stays empty, and a one-cell room with 1 is shaded. Tap a cell to shade it.",
  "tutChambers2": "A straight line of unshaded cells may not cross two room borders. The highlighted row runs through three rooms, and two of them hold no shaded cell, so the third one must break the line. Finish the board.",
  "tutChambers3": "The unshaded cells must stay in one piece. Once its neighbour is shaded, the top-left cell's only way out is the cell below it, so that cell stays. Tap a cell twice to dot it (your note that it stays), then finish the board.",
  "tutChambers4": "Now a real board. Start with 0 rooms, rooms that need every cell they have left, and long lines through several rooms.",
  "tutChambersS1": "Count the ways a room can hold its shaded cells. The highlighted room is three cells long and holds 2, and shaded cells never touch, so only its two ends can be shaded. Shade them, then finish the board.",
  "tutChambersS2": "Try every way to fit a room's shaded cells: none may touch, and every long line through the room that only it can break must be broken. A cell shaded in every way is shaded, one never shaded stays. Also, a cell whose shading would cut the unshaded cells in two stays.",
  "tutChambersS3": "A hard board. When stuck, shade a cell and follow on: if a room gets too many shaded cells, a long line can't be broken, or some cells get cut off, that cell stays.",
  "exChambersFull": "{cell} stays: room {room} {count, plural, =0{holds no shaded cells} =1{already has its 1 shaded cell} other{already has all {count} of its shaded cells}}.",
