  "polesName": "Poles",
  "polesTagline": "Give each tile a + and a − end, or none, to match the edge counts",
  "polesRules": "• The grid is cut into dominoes. Each domino is either charged, with a + at one end and a − at the other, or blank.\n• Two + cells never touch side by side, and neither do two − cells.\n• The numbers left of and above the grid tell how many + cells each row and column holds; the numbers right of and below it count the − cells. On hard boards some numbers are hidden.\n\nTap a cell to cycle: + → − → dot (blank) → empty. Right-click cycles back. Slide across cells to set them all in one go. A long press fills in the other end of every domino you started (a − across from a +, a dot across from a dot) and dots the rest of each line that has all its + and − cells. Dots are optional: the puzzle is done once every + and − is in place. A number fades once its line has that many.",
  "tutPoles1": "The grid is cut into dominoes. Each one is either charged, with a + at one end and a − at the other, or blank. The numbers left and above count the + cells of each row and column, the numbers right and below count the − cells. Tap a cell to cycle +, −, dot (blank).",
  "tutPoles2": "Two + cells never touch side by side, and neither do two − cells. That tells you which way round a domino goes: its + can't sit next to another +. Finish the board.",
  "tutPoles3": "Add a line's two numbers: that many of its cells are charged. When the line already has that many, its other cells are blank; when it needs every cell that can still be charged, none of those is blank. Finish the board.",
  "tutPoles4": "Now a real board. Start with lines whose numbers are zero, or that need every cell they have, and remember that the other end of a domino is always the opposite.",
  "tutPolesS1": "Think through every way to fill one line: its numbers, its dominoes and the rule that like ends never touch leave only a few. A value that no way puts into a cell is ruled out there. Look at the long rows of this board.",
  "tutPolesS2": "A hard board: some numbers are hidden. When stuck, suppose a cell holds a + and follow on: if a line can't get its numbers or two like ends meet, that cell holds no +.",
  "tagCharge": "plus, minus, positive, negative, charge, electric, polarity, attract, repel",
  "exPolesPartner": "{cell} is {value}: the other end of its domino, {other}, is {opposite}.",
